/T (Disability, then, is not merely a medical condition or a personal tragedy. It is a socially produced, fictional construct, that is upheld by economic structures, medicalisation, and through institutions of power that place profit over people. And yet, while disability is produced collectively, it is experienced individually and endured as if it were a personal misfortune rather than an intentional structural outcome. )
/E (Disability, then, is not merely a medical condition or a personal tragedy. It is a socially produced, fictional construct, that is upheld by economic structures, medicalisation, and through institutions of power that place profit over people. And yet, while disability is produced collectively, it is experienced individually and endured as if it were a personal misfortune rather than an intentional structural outcome. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
