/E (When I was given semi-solids as a 4-month old baby, that was when I had my first incident of food allergies. I reacted to pulses such that I had rashes and difficulty breathing. A few months later, my parents heard my first wheeze as I reacted to the dust and red soil being carried by the wind in Matheran - a hill-station. As an infant, my parents knew that consuming any allergen would cause itching on my tongue, lips and skin rashes. However, little did they know that far worse was yet to come. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [1]
