/E (Reality television frequently manages this stigma by transforming disabled contestants into inspirational figures. Instead of normalizing disability as one aspect of human diversity, shows frame contestants through narratives of perseverance, struggle, and triumph. These stories can generate emotional engagement among viewers, but they also reinforce the idea that disability must be overcome in order for individuals to be socially valued. )
/Pg 28 0 R
