/P 163 0 R
/E (Intersectionality teaches us that exclusion multiplies when identities overlap. Policies that address disability without considering these layered disadvantages risk benefiting only a privileged minority. )
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
377 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 163 0 R
/E (For example, accessible infrastructure in cities is valuable, but what of disabled persons in remote villages without transportation? Scholarships are meaningful, but what of those who drop out early due to discrimination? Inclusion must therefore be contextual and sensitive to social hierarchies. Community-level data, participatory planning, and representation of marginalized voices in decision-making are critical.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
