/E (Community-based rehabilitation \(CBR\) models emphasize participation, local resource mobilization, and empowerment. Instead of isolating individuals in institutions, CBR strengthens community capacity to support diverse needs. Peer networks and disability-led organizations further amplify voices and promote leadership. )
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
394 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 165 0 R
/E (Religious institutions, youth clubs, and neighbourhood associations can serve as platforms for awareness and solidarity. Inclusion must be woven into everyday community life rather than confined to specialized programs. )
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
