/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 166 0 R
/E (Social inclusion requires a shift from a charity-based model to a rights-based framework. Persons with disabilities are not beneficiaries of goodwill; they are citizens entitled to equality. Families are not burdens; they are partners. Communities are not passive observers; they are agents of change. )
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
403 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 166 0 R
/E (In the end, inclusion is measured not by the number of ramps constructed or schemes launched, but by whether a child with a disability can dream without fear, whether a woman with a disability can walk safely in her neighbourhood, whether a caregiver feels supported rather than isolated, and whether society sees disability not as deficiency but as diversity.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
404 0 obj
<<
