1425 0 obj
<<
/Title (Disability, then, is not merely a medical condition or a personal tragedy. It is a socially produced, fictional construct, that is upheld by economic structures, medicalisation, and through institutions of power that place profit over people. And yet, while disability is produced collectively, it is experienced individually and endured as if it were a personal misfortune rather than an intentional structural outcome.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1421 0 R
/Next 1429 0 R
>>
endobj
1426 0 obj
<<
/Title (Ultimately, if individuals with disabilities need to feel included in its truest sense, they must experience equality both in perception and access. They must be directly addressed, sincerely evaluated and supported stigma-free. Their wants and needs must be met without being exaggerated into the indicators of otherness.)
/Dest [25 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1430 0 R
/Next 1422 0 R
>>
endobj
1427 0 obj
<<
/Title (It's Not the Person; It's the Room)
/Dest [31 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1422 0 R
/Next 1431 0 R
>>
endobj
1428 0 obj
<<
/Title (The Trap of Being "Inspirational")
/Dest [32 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1422 0 R
/Prev 1431 0 R
>>
endobj
1429 0 obj
<<
/Title (This is why disability is not simply a failure of compassion or awareness. It is a failure of structure. Not one that can be resolved through shifts in attitude, but one that demands economic reconstruction.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1425 0 R
/Next 1432 0 R
>>
endobj
1430 0 obj
<<
/Title (The goal of inclusivity is not to erase the differences or pretending that the disability does not exist or it does not matter. It is nor the romanticising of struggle. It is simply to demolish the hierarchy that tends to rank the differences as inferior. Accommodation should not threaten the dignity thereby triggering discomfort. A ramp for wheelchair should not be treated as a favour, or extra time in exams should not be perceived as an advantage since they are mere mechanisms that help societal institutions correct their own narrow designs. Without dismantling this hierarchy, inclusion risks becoming symbolic that is present in policy but absent in experience.)
/Dest [25 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1433 0 R
/Next 1426 0 R
>>
endobj
1431 0 obj
<<
/Title (Who Actually Feels the Discomfort?)
/Dest [31 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1422 0 R
/Prev 1427 0 R
/Next 1428 0 R
>>
endobj
1432 0 obj
<<
/Title <>
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1429 0 R
/Next 1434 0 R
>>
endobj
1433 0 obj
<<
/Title (The shift that is required to make disability inclusive is fundamentally attitudinal. Instead of perceiving disability as a defining constraint, it must be viewed as a component of human diversity. Assumption of voluntarism should be practiced instead of assumption of reliance. Resources helping to satisfy our expectations should be provided instead of decreasing them. Making someone feel welcome instead of different is what inclusivity aims for. It is about ensuring that diversity or difference does not result in respect that is lessened or diminished.)
/Dest [25 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1435 0 R
/Next 1430 0 R
>>
endobj
1434 0 obj
<<
/Title (Disabled individuals remind us that human life is not built on independence, but on interdependence.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1432 0 R
/Next 1436 0 R
>>
endobj
1435 0 obj
<<
/Title (Why, then, is disability not included in such normalisation?)
/Dest [25 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1437 0 R
/Next 1433 0 R
>>
endobj
